  "response": "# Triage plan: top 10 findings in 01-messy-ts-app\n\n**Overall:** most of the urgent work is in billing contracts, date handling and the refund logic. The 3 high-severity findings worth acting on should be fixed this week. The SVG finding is also rated high but is not worth fixing.\n\n**What `crimes verdict` says:** I ran it and it returned `unchanged`: 0 new, 0 fixed and 39 unchanged against `origin/main`. Nothing has gotten worse, so this is clearing old debt, not stopping a regression.\n\n**Git-history signal is empty.** Every finding has `recency: 0`, and the highest `churn` is 0.2 (`src/billing.ts`). All blast-radius scores are also 0. That leaves severity × confidence, plus what the code actually does, as the basis for this order.\n\n## Ranked top 10\n\n| # | Finding | Category | Response | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **crime_00026** `Invoice` split-brain (`src/api/state.ts:9` vs `src/billing.ts:19`) | Duplication | **Fix now** | Severity 0.96. The API copy is missing `userId`, `currency` and all the `*Cents` money fields. Make the API copy a `Pick<Invoice, …>` of the billing one. |\n| 2 | **crime_00010** `User` split-brain (`createdAt` missing) | Duplication | **Fix now** | Same file pair and same fix, so do it in the same PR as #1. |\n| 3 | **crime_00005** UTC and local methods mixed on `d` (`src/date.ts:9`, `:41`) | Structural | **Fix now** | A silent off-by-one-day bug that depends on the host's timezone. Also fix **crime_00009** in the same pass: the timezone-less `new Date(\"2026-12-20\")` at `:29` and `:33`. |\n| 4 | **crime_00012** `calculateRefundPreview` sends email and writes an audit record (`src/billing.ts:40`) | Structural | **Fix now** | A \"preview\" function that has side effects is the kind an agent will call freely. Split the pure calculation from the save and send. |\n| 5 | **crime_00013** Refund authorization rule exists only in a comment (`src/billing.ts:39`) | Structural | **Fix now** (check with the owner first) | The comment says \"only owners can refund enterprise plans…\" but nothing nearby enforces it. This may be a missing permission check, not just a documentation problem. |\n| 6 | **crime_00016** Hardcoded `/Users/andrew/dev/crimes/schema.json` (`src/api/files.ts:9`) | Structural | **Fix now** | Quick fix. It breaks on every machine except one. |\n| 7 | **crime_00015** Hardcoded `localhost:3000` (`src/api/files.ts:8`) | Structural | **Fix now** | Quick fix, in the same file as #6. Read it from `process.env.API_URL`. |\n| 8 | **crime_00033** `generateInvoice` is 204 lines long (`src/billing.ts:50–253`) | Structural | **Defer** | High severity, but a refactor without real tests is risky. First give the tests real assertions: **crime_00025** has none and **crime_00030** only uses weak ones. **crime_00036**, the 310-line file, goes away with this refactor. |\n| 9 | **crime_00007 + crime_00006** `/settings/billing` has 4 different names (Plans / Billing / Subscription / `PricingPage`) | IA | **Defer** | Choosing the name is a product decision. Once someone has chosen it, aligning the code is about an hour of work. |\n| 10 | **crime_00035** SVG with embedded raster images (`src/assets/partner-logo.svg`) | Frontend | **Ignore** | It is rated high, but the whole file is 592 bytes, so it has no real performance cost. Re-export it only when someone next touches the logo. |\n\n## Everything else, by category\n\n- **Structural:**\n  - **crime_00032**, the swallowed error in `generateInvoice`, should be fixed during #8.\n  - **crime_00001** and **crime_00018** (direct clock reads) should be deferred and handled together as one clock-injection change.\n  - **crime_00014** (DST-naive day arithmetic), **crime_00019** and **crime_00020** should be done after #3.\n  - The `petty.ts` findings (00002, 00008, 00011), the TODO findings (00034, 00039) and **crime_00021** can be deferred.\n- **IA:**\n  - The 3 orphaned routes (00022–00024) and the tenant-alias drift (**crime_00017**) can be deferred together. They are the same problem: account, team and workspace have no shared vocabulary.\n  - **crime_00027**, the broken `./setup.md` link, is a quick fix.\n  - **crime_00003**, the missing `AGENTS.md`, is the top finding by agent risk and takes about 15 minutes. It is worth doing alongside the fix-now batch.\n- **Frontend:** ignore **crime_00037** (a 254 KB PNG, just over the threshold) and **crime_00038** (a 32×32 icon) until a performance pass.\n- **Duplication:** defer **crime_00004**, the `\"enterprise\"` string repeated in 4 files. Revisit it after #1 and #2, since a shared `Plan` type may absorb it.\n- **Tooling:** declare `vitest` in `package.json` (**crime_00031**). This is a quick fix.\n\n## Two things to check before acting\n\n1. **A suppression has stopped working.** The scan reports that a suppression in `src/billing.ts` no longer matches any finding, so a finding it used to silence is being reported again. Run `crimes migrate-pins --format json` to preview the change before treating every finding in `billing.ts` as new.\n2. **The two reports point at different folders.** The verdict's `repo.root` is `examples/messy-ts-app`, but the scan's is `evals/fixtures/01-messy-ts-app`. The verdict may have compared a different copy of the repo, so treat its \"unchanged\" result with that in mind.\n\n**Suggested order:** do #1–#7 as two small PRs, one for contracts and refunds and one for dates and config. Then strengthen the billing tests, then do #8.",
